# Never resolve a package version published less than three days ago.
#
# Two reasons, one setting:
#
# 1. Supply chain. A compromised release is usually yanked within hours. Three
#    days of distance means we are not the ones who find it.
#
# 2. Dependabot. Its updater runs pnpm with this same 4320-minute gate. If
#    package.json carries a range whose only satisfying versions are younger
#    than the gate, pnpm cannot resolve the manifest and *every* dependency in
#    the job dies with ERR_PNPM_NO_MATURE_MATCHING_VERSION. That silently
#    killed dependency PRs on this repo through September 2026 (LAC-4109):
#    `motion: ^13.3.0` on Sep 16, `fumadocs-core: ^16.15.17` on Oct 1, both
#    floors written a day or two after those versions shipped. Matching the
#    gate here means pnpm can no longer write a floor Dependabot cannot read.
#
# Only resolution is gated. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (what Vercel runs)
# installs the versions already in the lockfile and is unaffected.
#
# Need a brand new release sooner, usually a security patch? Add that one
# package to `minimumReleaseAgeExclude` rather than lowering this number:
# https://pnpm.io/settings#minimumreleaseageexclude
minimum-release-age=4320

# Keep registry tokens out of this file: it is committed. Use ~/.npmrc or an
# NPM_TOKEN in the environment instead.
